                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-9" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Services"  ><h5>Lending Services</h5>
<p>The library at the headquarters caters to more than 3000 plus members comprising academic and administrative staff of the university, retired staff, consultants, Ph.D. students and other project staff of the University. Lending service is available to all the permanent staff of the University.</p>
<h5>Reprography Services</h5>
<p>The readers can get the Xerox of interested articles or chapters from the library documents. The service is available for IGNOU staff and other visitors on nominal charges of Re.1/per page.</p>

<h5>Reading and Reference Services</h5>
<p>The library has a very good collection of latest reference material comprising encyclopaedias, dictionaries, yearbooks, directories, statistical sources, geographical sources etc. Reference and information service is provided to the members as and when requested.</p>
<h5>OPAC (Online Public Access Catalogue) Service</h5>
<p>The Central Library of IGNOU is fully computerized. The Complete catalogue of the library is available through Web-OPAC. The information can be browsed and downloaded from anywhere.<br>
Click here for:<a href="https://libraryopac.ignou.ac.in/" target="_blank"> Central Library OPAC (https://libraryopac.ignou.ac.in/)</a><br>
Click here for:<a href="http://rcscopac.ignou.ac.in/" target="_blank"> RCs/SCs Library OPAC (http://rcscopac.ignou.ac.in/)</a>

</p>
<h5>Online Services</h5>
<p>Library subscribes to various online databases including e-books, journals, indexes, bibliographies, Statistical Reports etc. </p>
<h5>Institutional Membership Services</h5>
<p>IGNOU Library has Membership of British Council Library (BCL) New Delhi, Indian Library Association (ILA), New Delhi and Indian Institute of Public Administration (IIPA), New Delhi. The registered members can avail library facilities from these Institutions. In order to get the reference, reading and Lending Services (through ILL) from these libraries, registered members of the Central Library can collect the Membership card of the institution from Central Library which in turn to be shown at concerned Library for availing the services.</p>
<h5>DELNET Services
</h5>
<p>Library is a member of Developing Library Network (DELNET) which provides services like browsing of Union Catalogues, Inter Library Loan and Document Delivery Services. Interested Readers can access the Catalogues of other Libraries through DELNET. Password of DELNET is available at Central and RCs Libraries.</p><br>
